    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a4e4d475-322a-502c-a94b-ae7c57304f47",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}$ on $X?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the second row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim{\\small \\begin{bmatrix}-1+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(-2) & 1+(3)(7) \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 & 22 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
