      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -3 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim{\\small \\begin{bmatrix}9+(4)(6) & -3+(4)(-8) & -8+(4)(-1) \\\\ -6 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}33 & -35 & -12 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
